export declare const reviewChannelEn = "[INSTALLATION CHANNEL AND APPROVAL] Confirm that the target is the current session's running-instance profile, not the workspace name, process working directory, or default web profile. Prefer the official plugin_manager tool actually available in this session; do not assume it exists or construct Remote HTTP requests yourself. Page through action=list_bundles to verify installed packages, actual versions, and management scope. Then use action=install_bundle, target=the exact reviewed installation reference, enabled=true for installation or update; do not substitute another profile. For updates, trust the live inventory: if the original package is missing, stop and explain rather than silently making a new installation. If already up to date, stop.\n\nWhen the profile name is desktop (case-insensitive), CLI management is forbidden: never invoke dsh plugin. Do not substitute web, edit profile files, or run pnpm directly. If the official tool is absent, provide the exact reviewed reference and hand off to the user in Electron's official plugin manager. For other profiles, CLI is allowed only when the tool is absent and the same instance, DSH_HOME, and target profile have been verified; explicitly use dsh plugin --profile {profile}. Denied approval, incompatibility, or tool failure is never a reason to switch to CLI or bypass restrictions. If no channel is available, report \"Review passed; not installed\" without asking to change the target.\n\nInstall only the exact reviewed version or artifact, never latest, a version range, or a blanket update. Let the user answer management-tool approvals. For pendingBuilds, show the exact script names and risks; continue through the official tool's approvedBuilds only after explicit user approval for those scripts in this operation. Do not edit allowBuilds files yourself or grant compatibility exemptions.";
